build: 2026-06-28 v10.76.39 (rPPG: trust the confident autocorrelation)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.38. Smooths the camera heart-rate (rPPG) reading. Device logs
  showed the published BPM jumping 132 → 100 → 79 → 76 while a strong, steady pulse
  fundamental sat at 75–79 the whole time — the discrete peak-counter was being fooled by
  the dicrotic notch (a small second bump per heartbeat) and over-counting by ~1.3–1.7×.
  That's a NON-octave error, so the existing ×2/×0.5 octave guard couldn't catch it.
  Fix: a new `autoTrust` step gently pulls the reading toward the autocorrelation
  fundamental WHEN that periodicity is confident (acf > 0.55), weighted by its strength
  and capped at 50 % per window — so peak-count noise can't yank the number around while a
  clean pulse is being ignored, yet a genuine heart-rate change (or a low-SNR window where
  autocorrelation is weak) still leads. Pure helper, fully unit-tested, on the camera
  analysis path only (NOT audio/render/launch) — cannot affect the black-screen surface.
  Test: 10.76.39 → Well ▸ camera rPPG, finger on lens: the BPM should settle and hold
  steady instead of jumping by 20–50 between updates. Still launches straight to Studio.
